=== Relationships and family ===
Dharmendra married Prakash Kaur at the age of 19 in 1954, before he entered the film industry. It was an arranged marriage.<ref>{{cite news |title=Bobby Deol Reportedly Attacked Hema Malini with a Knife After Dharmendra's 2nd Marriage; Here's What Prakash Kaur Said on the Matter! |url=https://daily.bhaskar.com/news/ENT-BOW-dharmendra-hema-controversy-5440408-PHO.html |access-date=13 February 2020 |work=dailybhaskar |date=16 October 2016 |language=en |archive-date=13 February 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200213180023/https://daily.bhaskar.com/news/ENT-BOW-dharmendra-hema-controversy-5440408-PHO.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> The couple became parents to two sons, [[Sunny Deol]] and [[Bobby Deol]], both film actors; and two daughters, Vijeta (born in 1962) and Ajeeta (born in 1966).<ref>{{cite news |title=Dharmendra's family tree explained: Meet the actor's 6 children, 13 grandchildren, other members of Deol clan |url=https://www.financialexpress.com/life/entertainment-dharmendras-family-tree-explained-meet-the-actors-6-children-13-grandchildren-other-members-of-deol-clan-4054553/lite/ |work=The Financial Express |date=24 November 2025 |access-date=24 November 2025}}</ref> Throughout his life, Dharmendra spent most of his time with Kaur, while Malini lived independently with her daughters with him, often visiting Malini and their daughters.<ref>{{cite news |title=Dharmendra Dies At 89: A Look At His Marriages With Prakash Kaur And Hema Malini |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/dharmendra-dies-at-89-a-look-at-his-marriages-with-prakash-kaur-and-hema-malini-9608282 |work=NDTV |date=24 November 2025 |access-date=25 November 2025}}</ref>

After moving to [[Bombay]] and entering films, Dharmendra married [[Hema Malini]], which caused controversy at the time since he was already married. Rumours began to circulate about Dharmendra and Hema Malini converting to [[Islam]] for this wedding.<ref>{{cite news|title=Dharmendra or "Dilawar Khan?"|url=http://www.milligazette.com/Archives/2004/16-30Jun04-Print-Edition/163006200433.htm|access-date=18 June 2016|publisher=[[Milli Gazette]]|date=30 June 2004|quote=When his political rivals brought the issue to the notice of election authorities and the general public, he denied his conversion to Islam and change of name.|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160624093107/http://www.milligazette.com/Archives/2004/16-30Jun04-Print-Edition/163006200433.htm|archive-date=24 June 2016|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="converted">{{cite news|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/photo-features/celebrities-who-converted-to-islam/photostory/30985640.cms|title=Celebrities who converted to Islam|work=[[The Times of India]]|access-date=23 August 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170227231411/http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/Celebrities-who-converted-to-Islam/photostory/30985640.cms|archive-date=27 February 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2004, during a political campaign, when the rumours began to circulate again, Dharmendra asserted that he remained a [[Hindus|Hindu]],<ref name="ArabNews_Religion">{{Cite web |last=Suhrawardy |first=Nilofar |date=19 April 2004 |title=Dharmendra's Past Haunts His Present |url=https://www.arabnews.com/node/247932 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20040708094935/http://www.arabnews.com/?page=4&section=0&article=43427&d=19&m=4&y=2004 |archive-date=8 July 2004 |website=[[Arab News]] |quote=I am a Hindu. The question of my having ever changed religion does not exist.}}</ref> the family being [[Arya Samaj]]i.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Deols don't believe in superstitions |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/deols-dont-believe-in-superstitions/articleshow/4680292.cms |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241210085704/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/deols-dont-believe-in-superstitions/articleshow/4680292.cms |archive-date=10 December 2024 |work=[[The Times of India]] |date=21 June 2009 |access-date=29 December 2024 |quote=They [Dharmendra and Sunny Deol] said, 'We keep any kind of superstition at bay. Being followers of the Arya Samaj system, we bring in positive energy by doing good deeds for the good of others.'}}</ref> He and Malini starred together in a number of movies in the early 1970s, including ''[[Sholay]]''.<ref>{{cite news|title=Hema Malini on 35th wedding anniversary|url=http://www.mid-day.com/articles/love-is-togetherness-hema-malini-on-35th-wedding-anniversary/16181170|access-date=2 May 2015|work=[[Mid-Day]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170921114842/http://www.mid-day.com/articles/love-is-togetherness-hema-malini-on-35th-wedding-anniversary/16181170|archive-date=21 September 2017|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Dharmendra – Action King: Personal life|url=http://www.indianexpress.com/pictureStory.php?galId=1101&pg=4&view=4|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130126142727/http://www.indianexpress.com/pictureStory.php?galId=1101&pg=4&view=4|url-status=dead|archive-date=26 January 2013|work=The Indian Express|access-date=2 July 2011}}</ref> The couple had two daughters, [[Esha Deol]] (born in 1981) and Ahana Deol (born in 1985). His grandson, [[Bobby Deol|Bobby Deol's]] younger son, is also named "Dharam", after him.<ref name="grand1">{{cite news |last1=Goyal |first1=Divya |title=Viral: The Internet Is Crushing On Bobby Deol's Son Aryaman |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/viral-the-internet-is-crushing-on-bobby-deols-son-aryaman-1984709 |access-date=27 July 2022 |work=NDTV |date=29 January 2019 |archive-date=29 January 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190129114638/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/viral-the-internet-is-crushing-on-bobby-deols-son-aryaman-1984709 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Dharmendra had a farmhouse in [[Lonavala]], where he lived during his final years. His family resides in [[Juhu]], Mumbai.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 June 2021 |title=Dharmendra shares idyllic early morning views from his farmhouse. Watch video |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/dharmendra-shares-idyllic-early-morning-views-from-his-farmhouse-watch-video-101622608247977.html |access-date=22 August 2023 |website=Hindustan Times |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=राजाओं जैसी जिंदगी जीते हैं धर्मेंद्र, देखिए उनके 100 एकड़ में फैले आलीशान फार्महाउस की INSIDE तस्वीरें |url=https://www.amarujala.com/photo-gallery/entertainment/bollywood/dharmendra-lavish-100-acre-lonavala-farmhouse-inside-pictures |access-date=11 June 2024 |website=[[Amar Ujala]] |language=hi |archive-date=11 June 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240611123433/https://www.amarujala.com/photo-gallery/entertainment/bollywood/dharmendra-lavish-100-acre-lonavala-farmhouse-inside-pictures |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Dharmendra Farmhouse Pics: मुंबई की भीड़ से दूर लोनावला में बना है धर्मेंद्र का आलीशान फार्महाउस देखिए Inside तस्वीरें |url=https://www.abplive.com/photo-gallery/entertainment/bollywood-dharmendra-lonavala-luxury-farmhouse-inside-photos-see-here-2297662 |access-date=11 June 2024 |website=[[ABP Live]] |date=2 January 2023 |language=hi |archive-date=11 June 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240611123616/https://www.abplive.com/photo-gallery/entertainment/bollywood-dharmendra-lonavala-luxury-farmhouse-inside-photos-see-here-2297662 |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2023, Dharmendra lamented that Bollywood neglected his family and never appreciated Deol family's contributions to [[Cinema of India|Indian cinema]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 August 2023 |title=इंडस्ट्रीचं देओल कुटुंबाकडे दुर्लक्ष? अनेक वर्षांनंतर धर्मेंद्र अखेर व्यक्त झालेच |trans-title=Industry neglected Deol family? After many years Dharmendra expressed himself. |url=https://www.tv9marathi.com/entertainment/industry-never-recognised-deol-family-said-dharmendra-1003512.html |access-date=22 August 2023 |website=TV9 Marathi |language=mr |archive-date=22 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230822103214/https://www.tv9marathi.com/entertainment/industry-never-recognised-deol-family-said-dharmendra-1003512.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Dharmendra's relatives in the film industry include his paternal cousin and [[Punjabi cinema|Punjabi]] actor [[Veerendra]],<ref name=":02">{{cite news |journal=[[The Times of India]]|date=18 June 2019|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/videos/entertainment/regional/punjabi/film-on-dharmendras-cousin-veerendra-singh-who-was-shot-dead-during-shoot/videoshow/69845987.cms|title=Film on Dharmendra's cousin Veerendra Singh, who was shot dead during shoot|publisher=[[Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd.]]|access-date=31 October 2021|archive-date=17 August 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240817131520/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/videos/entertainment/regional/punjabi/film-on-dharmendras-cousin-veerendra-singh-who-was-shot-dead-during-shoot/videoshow/69845987.cms|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="IEVeerendarSingh2024">{{cite news
 |title=Months after Amar Singh Chamkila's murder, Dharmendra's cousin and Punjabi superstar Veerendar Singh was killed in Punjab. Both cases were never solved|url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/months-after-amar-singh-chamkilas-murder-dharmendras-cousin-and-punjabi-superstar-veerendar-singh-was-killed-in-punjab-both-cases-were-never-solved-9271434/|work=The Indian Express|date=15 April 2024|access-date=29 November 2025|location=Chennai}}</ref> his maternal cousin director-producer [[Guddu Dhanoa]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://mumbaimirror.indiatimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/this-week-that-year-birthday-boy-dharmendra-on-his-love-affair-with-cinema/articleshow/66994200.cms|title=Birthday boy Dharmendra on his love affair with cinema|website=Mumbai Mirror|date=8 December 2018|last=Bhattacharya|first=Roshmila|quote=Dharamji’s cousin, Guddu Dhanoa, says he’s proud to have a brother who’s so handsome.}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/dharmendra-discharged-from-hospital-filmmaker-and-cousin-guddu-dhanoa-visits-his-home-reveals-actor-is-recovering-well/articleshow/125272436.cms|title=Dharmendra discharged from hospital: Filmmaker and cousin Guddu Dhanoa visits his home, reveals actor is recovering well|date=12 November 2025|website=[[Times of India]]}}</ref> as well his nephew [[Abhay Deol]], son of his younger brother Ajit Deol (d. 2015) who was an actor in both Hindi and Punjabi cinema.<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 October 2015|title=Dharmendra's Brother, Bollywood Veteran Ajit Singh Deol Dies|url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/dharmendras-brother-bollywood-veteran-ajit-singh-deol-dies-1235891|website=[[NDTV]]}}</ref> Dharmendra launched Abhay Deol through his production house Vijayta Films in 2005 with ''[[Socha Na Tha]]'', which was also [[Imtiaz Ali (director)|Imtiaz Ali]]'s directorial debut. His brothers-in-law, through his sisters, were both producers: Sher Jung Singh Punchhe, who had produced ''Satyakam'' among others;<ref>{{cite news
 |last=Upadhyaya|first=Amit|title=Try watching 'Satyakam' in the age of post-truth, fake news and incorruptible leaders|url=https://theprint.in/feature/reel-take/try-watching-satyakam-in-the-age-of-post-truth-fake-news-and-incorruptible-leaders/86162/|publisher=|date=22 July 2018|access-date=29 November 2025|quote=So personal the project was for even Dharmendra, who gave his finest performance here, that the film was produced by his brother-in-law Sher Singh Jung Punchhe.|work=[[ThePrint]]}}</ref> and Bikram Singh Dehal (d. 2019), who had produced movies starring Dharmendra as well Sunny Deol's debut film, ''Betaab'' (1983).<ref>{{cite news
 |last=|first=|title=Bikram Singh Dehal Dead|url=https://filminformation.com/featured/bikram-singh-dehal-dead-16-august-2019/|publisher=|date=16 August 2019|access-date=29 November 2025|work=[[Komal Nahta|Film Information]]}}</ref>

===Health issues and death===
In 2010, Dharmendra had quit drinking alcohol after what he called a "health scare." He was previously known for his [[Alcoholism|alcohol addiction]], even being called "the biggest boozer in Bollywood", as he would drink up to 12 bottles a day.<ref>{{cite news |date=8 August 2024 |title=When Dharmendra reacted to being called the biggest boozer in Bollywood: 'Mera liver bahot strong hai' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/when-dharmendra-reacted-to-being-called-the-biggest-boozer-in-bollywood-mera-liver-bahot-strong-hai/articleshow/112361933.cms |access-date=24 November 2025 |work=The Times of India |publisher=TOI Entertainment Desk}}</ref>

Between 2015 and 2020, he had multiple health issues, including [[back pain]], [[muscle strain]], and weakness, which occasionally required hospitalisation. In 2025, Dharmendra underwent a [[Corneal transplantation|corneal transplant surgery]] after the [[cornea]] of his left eye was damaged.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/dharmendra-undergoes-eye-graft-interacts-with-paparazzi-with-bandaged-eye-calls-himself-strong-101743492513526.html|title=Dharmendra undergoes eye graft, interacts with paparazzi with bandaged eye; calls himself strong: 'Abhi bahut damm hai'|work=Hindustan Times|first=Ananya|last=Das|date=1 April 2025|access-date=24 November 2025}}</ref>

He had also been hospitalised on 31 October 2025 at the [[Breach Candy Hospital]] in Mumbai due to breathing difficulties. He was admitted to the ICU for observation and was discharged within a few hours once all his vital parameters stabilised.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/actor-dharmendra-discharged-from-breach-candy-hospital-10360455/lite/|title=Dharmendra Health Update Today: Veteran actor discharged from hospital, family statement says 'actor to continue recovery at home'|work=The Indian Express|date=12 November 2025|access-date=24 November 2025}}</ref>

On 10 November 2025, Dharmendra was again admitted to Breach Candy Hospital after complaining of respiratory issues. His second wife, Hema Malini, shared on social media that he was under continuous medical supervision. According to reports, he was placed on ventilator support as his condition became critical. Several actors, politicians, and fans across the country expressed their concern and prayed for his speedy recovery.<ref name="auto2">{{cite web | last=Kanetkar | first=Riddhima | title=After Esha Deol, Hema Malini DENIES reports of Dharmendra's death, accuses media of spreading 'false news': 'What is happening is unforgivable' | website=DNA India | date=11 November 2025 | url=https://www.dnaindia.com/bollywood/report-after-esha-deol-hema-malini-denies-reports-of-dharmendra-death-accuses-media-of-spreading-false-news-what-is-happening-is-unforgivable-3187794 | access-date=11 November 2025}}</ref>

On 11 November 2025, rumours began circulating on social media and several news channels claiming that Dharmendra had died. The reports spread rapidly, with many media outlets broadcasting the unverified news. His death rumours flooded the internet after Indian Defence Minister [[Rajnath Singh]] and poet and lyricist [[Javed Akhtar]] even mourned his death in a post. Later, Hema Malini and daughter Esha Deol dismissed the rumours through their social media accounts, confirming that Dharmendra was alive and in stable condition. They condemned the spread of such false information, calling it completely unacceptable and&nbsp;irresponsible.<ref>{{cite web | title=Dharmendra Health Updates: Hema Malini and Esha Deol rubbish reports of the actor's death | website=The Times of India | date=11 November 2025 | url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/dharmendra-health-updates-legendary-actor-dharmendra-health-news-celebs-reaction/liveblog/125237495.cms | access-date=11 November 2025}}</ref><ref name="auto2"/><ref>{{Cite news |date=11 November 2025 |title=Esha Deol rubbishes Dharmendra death reports: 'My father is stable and recovering' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/esha-deol-rubbishes-dharmendra-death-reports-my-father-is-stable-and-recovering/articleshow/125238888.cms |access-date=11 November 2025 |work=[[The Times of India]]}}</ref>

Dharmendra died on 24 November 2025 at his residence in Mumbai, at the age of 89 following age-related illness, two weeks before his 90th birthday.<ref>{{Cite magazine |title=Veteran Actor Dharmendra Passes Away at 89 |url=https://www.filmfare.com/news/bollywood/veteran-actor-dharmendra-passes-away-at-89_-79088.html |magazine=Filmfare |date=24 November 2025 |access-date=24 November 2025}}</ref><ref name="BBC_24Nov2025">{{cite news |last=Pandey |first=Geeta |date=24 November 2025 |title=Dharmendra: Bollywood's 'He-Man' dies at 89 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cg66lv566kyo |work=BBC |access-date=24 November 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=24 November 2025 |title=Veteran actor Dharmendra passes away LIVE updates: Tributes pour in |url=https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/actor-dharmendra-death-bollywood-funeral-movies-live-updates-on-november-24-2025/article70265484.ece |access-date=24 November 2025 |work=The Hindu |language=en-IN |issn=0971-751X}}</ref> His last rites were held at the Pawan Hans crematorium in the [[Vile Parle]] area of Mumbai, with family members and numerous film-industry colleagues in attendance.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mukhopadhyay |first=Sounak |date=24 November 2025 |title=Dharmendra no more: Bollywood celebrities reach Pawan Hans crematorium in Vile Parle for his last rites {{!}} Watch videos |url=https://www.livemint.com/entertainment/dharmendra-no-more-hema-malini-reaches-pawan-hans-crematorium-in-vile-parle-for-his-last-rites-watch-video-11763974565174.html |work=Mint |access-date=25 November 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Pathak |first=Manish Kumar |date=24 November 2025 |title=Dharmendra's death: Hundreds throng Mumbai crematorium, triggering major traffic snarl on SV Road as Bollywood stars bid farewell |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/cities/mumbai/dharmendras-death-hundreds-crematorium-major-traffic-snarl-10383669/ |work=The Indian Express |access-date=25 November 2025}}</ref> Upon the release of ''[[Ikkis]]'' on 1 January 2026, his last film, tributes were paid to him along with his ''[[Sholay]]'' and [[Chupke Chupke (film)|''Chupke Chupke'']] co-star [[Asrani]], who died on 20 October 2025.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kumar |first1=Ritika |date=31 December 2025 |title='Ikkis is his salute': Sunny Deol pays heartfelt tribute to Dharmendra, calls film his gift to fans |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/sunny-deol-pays-heartfelt-tribute-to-dharmendra-calls-ikkis-his-gift-to-fans-101767181814870.html |work=Hindustan Times |access-date=28 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Arif |first1=Anas |date=1 January 2026 |title=Ikkis: Asrani shares one of his last screen appearances with Dharmendra, Sriram Raghavan pays a special tribute |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ikkis-asrani-one-last-film-dharmendra-sriram-raghavan-special-tribute-10450100/ |work=The Indian Express |access-date=28 February 2026}}</ref>

